    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d740">

                <pb facs="0813" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg801"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/1806: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Diplomatic Agent and Consul General at Tangier</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-12-18T13:00:00+01:00">December 18,
                            1940—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>90. My British colleague and my Dutch colleague have protested in writing to
                    Colonel Yuste against ejection of international administrators.</p>
                <pb facs="0814" n="802" xml:id="pg802"/>
                <p>The new Spanish administrator has written advising me and other colleagues of his
                    assumption of office.</p>
                <p>I understand that a Spanish Court of Justice will be instituted January 1 but
                    that Mixed Court will remain some months longer for the purpose of finishing
                    pending cases.</p>
                <p>Yuste is reported to be disposed to restrict his activities to military affairs.
                    He is stated to have said that all Moorish troops except 1,000 cavalry will
                    leave Tangier, their place is being taken by peninsular Spaniards in numbers to
                    constitute a total garrison of between 3 and 4 thousand. He denies arrival of
                    additional artillery.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
